ast-name>DOI, NOBUKAZU</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>HITACHI, LTD.</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>ISHIFUJI, TOMOAKI</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KUWAHARA, MIKIO</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>DOI NOBUKAZU</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>ISHIFUJI TOMOAKI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>KUWAHARA MIKIO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>DOI, NOBUKAZU</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>ISHIFUJI, TOMOAKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KUWAHARA, MIKIO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A terminal receives a specific signal transmitted from a base station of a cellular system, and the terminal performs positioning based on the base station information stored in the terminal. Specifically, a terminal (1) is provided with a memory (6), in which the position of a base station and the transmission timing information of a specific signal are stored. The timings of reception of signals from at least three stations are measured, and the position of the terminal is estimated from the differences between the transmission timing information and the timings of the received signals. Transmission, which consumes power greatly, from the terminal is decreased, and therefore the life of the battery of the terminal is prevented from being shortened.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, un terminal reçoit un signal spécifique transmis depuis une station de base d'un système cellulaire et effectue un positionnement sur la base des informations de la station de base stockées dans le terminal. Plus particulièrement, un terminal (1) est muni d'une mémoire (6) dans laquelle la position d'une station de base et les informations de synchronisation de la transmission d'un signal spécifique sont stockées. Les temps de réception des signaux provenant d'au moins trois stations sont mesurés, et la position du terminal est estimée à partir des différences entre les informations de synchronisation de la transmission et les temps de réception des signaux reçus. La transmission à partir du terminal, très gourmande en énergie, est réduite, ce qui préserve la durée de vie de l'accumulateur du terminal.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>